From ef145f78758dc3a8cc6cbdfe8eb427c9681ea8ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:16:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 219/270] debug_server: save a plain text report when the
 Debugger is missing

"Save report" hands the team over to the Debugger, which writes the
report. The Debugger does not exist for every architecture (not for ARM),
and then nothing was saved and the team was killed.

When it is missing, debug_server now writes the report itself to the
desktop: the reason the team stopped, the stack trace and registers of
that thread, the stack traces of the other threads, and the loaded
images. The stack trace printing is shared with the syslog output.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
---
